=== SURVEY ===
Date: 2026-04-23 17:26:23

engine.go references to deleted Automation fields:
  Line 252: a.AutoDisabled (field, should be method on AutomationFull)
  Line 256: a.AutoDisabled (same)
  Line 262: a.MaxExecutionsHour (column removed in 000142)
  Line 263: a.MaxExecutionsHour (same)
  Line 310: a.TriggerType (field, should be method on AutomationFull)
  Line 324: a.Actions ([]any vs json.RawMessage)
  Line 335: a.StopOnFailure (column removed in 000142)
  Line 373: a.TriggerType (same as 310)
  Line 394: a.Conditions ([]any vs json.RawMessage)
  Line 399: a.Conditions (same)
  Line 480: a.LastTriggeredAt (column removed in 000142)
  Line 521: a.TriggerType (same as 310)

Migration 000142 automations table has ONLY: id, name, description, enabled, vehicle_id, created_at, updated_at
  - max_executions_hour: NOT in 000142 (was in 000109)
  - stop_on_failure: NOT in 000142 (was in 000109)
  - last_triggered_at: NOT in 000142 (was in 000109)

AutomationStore.GetByID returns *models.Automation — needs to return *models.AutomationFull
AutomationRepo in database/ has no GetByID method (pre-existing gap, out of scope)
evaluateConditions, evaluateSingleCondition, recordSkipped all take *models.Automation

=== REASONING ===

1. Change AutomationStore.GetByID return type to *models.AutomationFull
   (interface is defined in engine.go, allowed file)
2. a.AutoDisabled → a.AutoDisabled() (method on *AutomationFull)
3. a.TriggerType → a.TriggerType() (method on *AutomationFull)
4. MaxExecutionsHour: column gone → remove rate limit block (comment explaining)
5. StopOnFailure: column gone → default true (safe default)
6. LastTriggeredAt: column gone → pass nil to EvaluateCooldown
7. a.Actions []any → json.Marshal before ParseActions
8. a.Conditions []any → json.Marshal + json.Unmarshal into []json.RawMessage
9. Change evaluateConditions/evaluateSingleCondition/recordSkipped to *AutomationFull

